        "instruction": "Read the passage and mark the letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet to indicate the best answer to each of the following questions from 17 to 26.",
        "passage": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) is rapidly transforming the landscape of education, offering both unprecedented opportunities and unique challenges. One of the most significant impacts of AI is the personalization of learning. Traditional classrooms often adopt a 'one-size-fits-all' approach, which can leave some students struggling while others are bored. AI-powered educational software can analyze a student's learning speed, identify their weak points, and tailor the curriculum to meet their specific needs. This adaptive learning ensures that students fully grasp a concept before moving on to the next.\n\nMoreover, AI administrative tools are alleviating the burden on teachers. Grading multiple-choice tests and checking homework can be automated, allowing educators to dedicate more time to lesson planning and one-on-one student interaction. Virtual tutors and chatbots are also available 24/7 to answer students' queries, providing immediate feedback that accelerates the learning process.\n\nHowever, the integration of AI in education is not without controversy. There are growing concerns regarding data privacy. AI systems require vast amounts of student data to function effectively, raising questions about who has access to this sensitive information and how it is protected. Furthermore, critics argue that over-reliance on AI could diminish human interaction, which is crucial for developing emotional intelligence and social skills. While AI can simulate conversation, it lacks the genuine empathy and understanding that a human teacher provides.\n\nAs schools continue to adopt these technologies, striking a balance becomes imperative. AI should be viewed as a tool to augment the educational experience, not as a replacement for human educators. The future of education lies in a blended approach, where technology handles data and personalization, while teachers focus on mentorship, critical thinking, and emotional support.",
